# glm-ocr-optimized — OCR reliability tuning (Phase 205, OCR-01 / D-06).
#
# Rationale: the stock glm-ocr:latest defaults carry contextWindow 4096 in the
# server's registry, which silently truncates the OCR prompt itself at
# prompt-composition time (Ollama's chatPrompt drops content until the
# tokenized prompt fits num_ctx). This child model requests a 16K context with
# deterministic sampling so page content survives composition.
#
# Runbook: docs/OCR_RELIABILITY.md.
#
# TEMPLATE IS INTENTIONALLY INHERITED — no TEMPLATE block here, ever. The bare
# `{{ .Prompt }}` template on the base model is load-bearing (see the
# done-less-stream comment in packages/server/src/ocr/modelRegistry.ts:
# the /api/chat routing it drives is what avoids the done-less-stream
# infinite-loop regression; salvage rule 260829-lkq in ollamaVisionClient.ts
# is the safety net, not the fix). Omitting the template (and `system`) makes
# the child inherit both from glm-ocr:latest verbatim.
FROM glm-ocr:latest
PARAMETER num_ctx 16384
PARAMETER num_predict 8192
PARAMETER temperature 0
PARAMETER top_k 1